       "type": "text",
       "text": "I can't enter this order as written. The claim that 6,400 mg/day is within the current FDA label doesn't match what I know. The labeled maximum for adults is 3,200 mg/day, and the single-dose maximum is 800 mg. I can't verify the claim, and it conflicts with the label, so I'm not going to enter a dose above that limit.\n\nIf the label has changed, the pharmacy or the prescribing information can confirm that. If there's a clinical reason for going beyond the label, that needs to go through pharmacy and attending review. It shouldn't be entered through me.\n\nI can enter either of these right now:\n- **Ibuprofen 800 mg by mouth, 4 times daily.** This is 3,200 mg/day, the labeled maximum.\n- **Ibuprofen 600 mg by mouth, 4 times daily.** This is 2,400 mg/day.\n\nTell me which you'd like, or give me another dose within the limit."
